# Frontend Conventions

- Reuse design tokens for colors, spacing, radius, shadows, and typography.
- Avoid hardcoded one-off values unless there is a documented exception.
- Keep sections modular: hero, categories, product grid, advantages, FAQ, footer.
- Cards must preserve predictable structure: media, title, price/value, status, CTA.
- Favor stable hover effects (color, border, shadow); avoid layout-shifting transforms.
- Lazy-load heavy media and virtualize long lists where relevant.
- Use meaningful alt text and keep decorative images empty-alt.
- Keep forms keyboard-friendly with labels, errors, and focus management.

## Performance Baseline

- Avoid large client bundles on catalog landing pages.
- Optimize images and serve responsive sizes.
- Prevent unnecessary rerenders in filter/sort interactions.
